;; Where each mirrored revision came from — and where that is UNKNOWN.
;;
;; Rev.5 is pinned (data/rev5/upstream.edn: URL, sha256, fetch date, encoding).
;; **Rev.4 IS NOT.** data/classes/*.json carries no source URL, no sha256 and no
;; fetch date; the README names only the UN landing page, and the git history is
;; a single squashed "chore: extract app repository". 428 files, provenance
;; unknown.
;;
;; That would be a documentation gap and nothing more, except that it is
;; MEASURABLY in conflict with what the UN serves today.

{:schema "un.isic.provenance.v1"
 :measured-at "2026-08-15"

 :rev5 {:pinned? true :record "data/rev5/upstream.edn"}

 ;; ⚠ SUPERSEDED IN PART, 2026-09-01. :what-the-mirror-actually-is below reached
 ;; the conclusion that data/classes "IS NOT THE UN'S ISIC REV.4" and belongs to
 ;; the NACE family. Measuring all 428 classes against BOTH references -- rather
 ;; than the 33 whose titles differed from one of them -- refutes that: 381 of
 ;; 428 titles (89%) match the UN's ISIC Rev.4 exactly, and the NACE
 ;; contamination is localised, 25 of its 47 classes in division 47 alone.
 ;; catalog.edn carries the replacement measurement, the pinned NACE
 ;; reference it was made against, and the per-code lists. What did NOT change:
 ;; the Rev.4 half is still unpinned, and its source address is still unknown.

 :rev4
 {:pinned? false
  :files 428
  :fields ["code" "nameEn" "group" "description" "includes"]
  :source-url :unknown
  :sha256 :unknown
  :fetched-at :unknown
  :git-history "single squashed commit b0028c6 'chore: extract app repository'"}

